# Local developer overrides. Copy to .env.local (gitignored) — never commit
# real secrets here. .env.local is loaded on top of .env by Next.js.

# --- Demo mode (frontend-only, dev-only) ---
# When "true" AND you are running `next dev` (NODE_ENV=development), every
# page under the authed app shell (/today, /chat, /agent-runs, /connections,
# etc.) works without Postgres, Redis, or Google OAuth — no sign-in required,
# all data comes from in-memory fixtures (src/lib/fixtures), and suggested
# actions / chat / approve-reject run against a simulated in-memory agent run
# instead of the real backend.
#
# Safety: this flag is read only through src/lib/demo.ts, which additionally
# requires NODE_ENV === "development". `next build` / `next start` always run
# with NODE_ENV=production, and NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the
# client bundle at build time — so a production build cannot contain a live
# demo-mode code path no matter what this variable is set to on the machine
# that runs it. Real Google OAuth and the real API routes are completely
# untouched by this flag; it only changes which implementation the frontend's
# lib/api.ts points at.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true
